    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d720">

                <pb facs="0883" n="871" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg871"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.0090/1508: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-02-22">February 22,
                        1943</date>.<lb/>[Received February 22—4:08 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1211. American interests Japan, exchange. Department’s 291, 4th. Swiss
                    representative Tokyo<anchor n="12" xml:id="d720-f1"/> reported telegraphically
                    February 18 that he insisted personally Japanese authorities examine proposals
                    contained telegram under reference and reply concerning safe conduct <pb
                        facs="0884" n="872" xml:id="pg872"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Gripsholm</hi> but Japanese Foreign Minister<anchor
                        n="13" xml:id="d720-f2"/> replied with generalities stating that Japan
                    favorable evacuation civilians as stated by Tani before Parliament but Foreign
                    Office remained silent concerning concrete measures taken or to be taken toward
                    new exchange.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d720-f1" n="12" xml:id="d720-f1-content">
                <p>Camille Gorgé, Swiss Minister in Japan.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d720-f2" n="13" xml:id="d720-f2-content">
                <p>Masayuki Tani.</p>
            </note>
